{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804666-a-life-without-cover","id":804666,"title":"A Life Without Cover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T13:30:00-08:00","id":804666,"title":"A Life Without Cover","content":"I was chewing on this idea today and didn't get anywhere meanigful with it, but wanted to open the topic up to the forum here anyway; what would you think of one of the Unchained whose goal in life was to live an existence free of a Cover, instead existing in their true form at all times? I can imagine a decent number of demons who dislike the prospect of spending the rest of their existence masquerading as a lowly human; while not Integrators, they accept that they are creatures of chrome and molded plastics, not flesh and blood, and wish to live without a mask. I figure it ties in well to the concept of raising Primum, as the Unchained grows further from the God-Machine's influence and into a unique creature, but then the logistics of how to escape constant Compromise rolls and hunter-killer Angels rears its ugly head. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:00:06-08:00","id":804681,"title":"","content":"I guess you could fly off through space until you find a place untouched by the God Machine, but it might be pretty boring.<br /> <br /> It's lonely out in space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:19:16-08:00","id":804697,"title":"","content":"I imagine Psychopomps don't even need to go too far into Primum, since so many must find being restricted to two arms awfully irritating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10825-crosswords","name":"Crosswords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:36:12-08:00","id":804712,"title":"","content":"Now I've got the idea for a advanced merit linked to the Sympathetic Stigmatic merit brewing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:46:32-08:00","id":804719,"title":"","content":"There are several ways to achieve this, sorta, easily modulated by Agenda and the scope of ambition. One is simply finding a place without the God-Machine influence - this might be extradimensional (move to the Hedge/Shadow/Underworld, etc, though these planes do have their difficulties) or even on earth. On a small scale, it's up to your ST as to whether assuming your true form in a bolthole (where time doesn't pass) constitutes compromise. There are also areas free of the Machine's influence, or at least whee it's attenuated (and you can make them the hard way), like Chernobyl and surrounds. If you're more ambitious you might want to suborn/design a piece of Infrastructure to protect you from compromise, you might want to kill the Machine so you can take your true form or make your own fiefdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:49:52-08:00","id":805126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804666-a-life-without-cover?p=804719#post804719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several ways to achieve this, sorta, easily modulated by Agenda and the scope of ambition. One is simply finding a place without the God-Machine influence - this might be extradimensional (move to the Hedge/Shadow/Underworld, etc, though these planes do have their difficulties) or even on earth. On a small scale, it's up to your ST as to whether assuming your true form in a bolthole (where time doesn't pass) constitutes compromise. There are also areas free of the Machine's influence, or at least whee it's attenuated (and you can make them the hard way), like Chernobyl and surrounds. If you're more ambitious you might want to suborn/design a piece of Infrastructure to protect you from compromise, you might want to kill the Machine so you can take your true form or make your own fiefdom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of these:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I'm not sure even the Hedge, Shadow, or Underworld would work - The Machine still has <i>some</i> influence (and presumably Infrastructure) there, just far less than the mortal world.</li> <li>This is talked about - that there are places in the world virtually devoid of the G-M's attention. But lists the problems as being without an Aether source, leaving the Demon vulnerable.</li> <li>Boltholes are kinda small, right? So the Demon in question would be confining themselves, likely alone, to a small room forever. Well, it is <i>a</i> Hell, I suppose...</li> <li>The Suborned Infrastructure is a nice idea. Of course, then the Demon has to defend said Infrastructure.</li> <li>Ah, the Saboteur's recruitment pitch. :-)</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T04:55:53-08:00","id":805151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804666-a-life-without-cover?p=805126#post805126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of these:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I'm not sure even the Hedge, Shadow, or Underworld would work - The Machine still has <i>some</i> influence (and presumably Infrastructure) there, just far less than the mortal world.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>As of Storytellers Guide the Hedge is actually a safe place for Demons.... sorta.... I mean, it's full of goblins still and you don't want to wander off the path into the thorns, but no God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:20:38-08:00","id":805159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/804666-a-life-without-cover?p=805126#post805126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of these:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>This is talked about - that there are places in the world virtually devoid of the G-M's attention. But lists the problems as being without an Aether source, leaving the Demon vulnerable.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course, being in demon form means you never run out of Aether (so actually you don't need a source if you're able to stay in your demon shape at all times), and Suborned Infrastructure is the best source of Aether, so the Marshals might just be onto somethin'. To return to the Chernobyl example, that place is just <i>lousy </i>with broken old Infrastructure, hence why it's so attractive to demons. Shame about the Exile and Pandorans, really... A general pattern with Hells that let you avoid the Machine is new problems, usually the locals, to contend with instead. <br /> <br /> Also, I rather love the image of an Inquisitor in a tiny bolthole/suborned Infrastructure hell... that's linked to their surveillance networks, so they never need to leave. <br /> <br /> There's also the option of a friendly Lare - though they don't protect you from compromise, they can provide Aether and, if you're lucky and do something from them, they might have your back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}